  "goodToKnow": "Das Sonnenlicht is sunlight: direktes Sonnenlicht, vor Sonnenlicht schützen (keep out of direct sunlight). Germany gets around 1,600 to 2,000 hours of sunshine a year, so many Germans take vitamin D in winter. Sunscreen shows a Lichtschutzfaktor (LSF, SPF). Der Sonnenschein is sunshine, and also a term of endearment: Na, mein Sonnenschein? It has no plural."
